    "name": "ConvKB",
    "description": "ConvKB is a novel embedding model proposed for knowledge base completion that advances state-of-the-art models by using a convolutional neural network to capture global relationships and transitional characteristics between entities and relations. In ConvKB, each triple is represented as a 3-column matrix. This matrix is fed into a convolution layer where multiple filters generate feature maps, which are then concatenated into a single feature vector. This vector generates a score by being multiplied with a weight vector via a dot product, and this score is used to predict the validity of the triple. Experiments showed that ConvKB achieves better link prediction performance than previous state-of-the-art models on the WN18RR and FB15k-237 benchmark datasets.",
